{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310620,"nonce":"H09aNigyLeUQRn2yeMeqE7ArlOk=","title":"2026-09-21 665d146e+196eeb1f (593-\u003e600): a static used as a VALUE returned a BOX where its type said Int (adapter ABI != lambda ABI); EVERY ...","message":"Found by the standing method: self-checking probes of ORDINARY Haxe\n(scratchpad/probe/S3, D2, TP1-8, AS1, M1). None of it was visible in any\nfailure list; `apply(compare,5,2)` returned 38639152064 on HEAD.\n\n- **Closure-value adapter** (vtables.rs `ensure_closure_value_adapter`): now\n  `(env, declared..) -\u003e declared`, like a lambda of the same type. The old\n  erased `(env,i64..)-\u003ei64` + BOXED result (5e40a9ed) only matched Dynamic\n  call sites; every TYPED call site read the box as the value.\n  `arr.sort(compare)`, `ArraySort.sort(a, compare)`, `var f = compare` fixed.\n- **IIFE**: `(function(f,o){..})(blub, {..})` types its params from the args\n  (calls.rs, `expected_lambda_params_stack`) — Issue6480 kept passing.\n- **Operator-use inference** for unannotated params (mod.rs\n  `collect_param_operator_uses`, `collect_param_copies`; wired in\n  classes.rs `param_types_from_uses`): arithmetic/compare/bit/`++`/`-x`/index\n  → Int; cond/`!p` → Bool; `var x:T = p`, `return p` (annotated) → T;\n  `var i = p` copies carry uses; `\"\"+p` → String ONLY if nothing else;\n  literal default → its type (`b = 4.25` was Dynamic → printed f64 bits).\n  Haxe's own rules verified with `$type` (`x * 1.5` makes x Int!).\n  `RAYZOR_PARAM_INFER_LOG=1` logs only the field-store path.\n- Lambda returned from a `:Void-\u003eDynamic` fn boxes its result\n  (`expected_lambda_return`, `lower_lambda_body` sets\n  `current_function_return_type` — lambdas used the ENCLOSING fn's before);\n  unsafe `cast e` to Dynamic boxes; `haxe_unbox_if_tag` opens a function box\n  at Let/return into a function type; `haxe_dynamic_truthy` for `if (dyn)`.\n\nA `Dynamic` in a type is as often a DECAY as a declaration: unannotated\nparam, unresolved type param (stdlib placeholder!), forward-declared return,\ncontext-less `cast`. Every rule \"value → Dynamic slot ⇒ box\" must ask WHERE\nthe Dynamic came from:\n- lambda return retyping: only from the ENCLOSING fn's declared return, never\n  from a formal's function type (Issue2378 boxed a String into Array\u003cS\u003e);\n- lambda body return type: only when declared Dynamic (Issue2874: a\n  `Null\u003cInt\u003e` lambda boxed what parseInt's callers read RAW);\n- `cast e`: adopt Class/Interface/TypeParameter/abstract-UNDERLYING context\n  as the target (Issue2835 `this.value = cast v` is a cast to T → BITCAST\n  the f64; Issue6656 `return cast value` in @:from is a cast to String);\n- T arg into a GENERIC callee's Dynamic formal stays raw (see\n  bugs_type_param_to_dynamic_and_isoftype_type_ids).\n\nDFS over same-class calls fixes forward-declared inferred returns\n(`cat(\"x\") != \"ax\"`) but made Template's `makeExpr` return `Void-\u003eDynamic`\n→ closure boxed at `var e1:Dynamic = ..` → `::if (n \u003e 2)::` took neither\nbranch. Retry after c3fb406. A renamed verbatim COPY of Template.hx in the\nuser module never reaches OpIf at all — not a faithful reproduction.\n\n`runtime/src/closure_entries.rs`: registry code-ptr → {slot, dynamic} entry.\nEvery closure target (lambda, adapter, method-ref thunk, mapped-static thunk,\ninner fn) gets `__closure_dyn_entry__*` `(env, box..)-\u003ebox` and, unless all\ndeclared types are 64-bit slots, `__closure_slot_entry__*` `(env,i64..)-\u003ei64`\n(vtables.rs `build_closure_entry`, kinds from the Haxe fn type via\n`closure_targets: BTreeMap\u003cIrFunctionId, Option\u003cTypeId\u003e\u003e`). Registered in\n`__vtable_init__`, which is now generated AFTER `__init__` (a static\ninitializer's lambda was missing otherwise — Issue6158). Dynamic call site\n(`indirect.rs lower_dynamic_closure_call`): box args, `haxe_closure_dynamic_view`,\ncall `(ptr..)-\u003eptr`, result in `boxed_value_regs`. Runtime `haxe_array_map/\nfilter/sort` call `closure_slot_code(fn_ptr)` → `[2.0,4.0].map(half)` correct.\n**Consumers assumed a Dynamic call result RAW**: a KNOWN box (boxed_value_regs)\nis now unboxed at return-into-concrete, at local/cross-module formals\n(`haxe_dynamic_to_slot` for erased T — `haxe_unbox_scalar_or_addr` keeps the\nBOX address for a String box, that was Issue6158's crash), and Let already did.\n**Mapped-static thunk (`Reflect.compare` as a value) took NO env** while every\nindirect call passes one — it has one now (it \"worked\" before only by an\naccident I never explained; RC1.hx probe). Also: a pushed function literal\ntypes `var arr = []` (Issue3792); a call through a function-typed PARAM types\nthe unannotated args (`callTyped(cmp:Int-\u003eInt-\u003eInt, x, y)`); lambda params\nget operator-use inference when no expected signature.\nTRAP: a `Dynamic` lambda param (untyped, no uses) is `Ptr(Void)` = same\nIrType as a class instance; the entry decides by the HAXE type, else treats\nPtr(Void) as Dynamic (pass the box through).\n\n- 5e6d0b3 lambda vs generic formal keeps T (`applyT((a,b)-\u003ea-b,5,2)`=0;\n  String sort compares pointers).\n- Template `::if isMale::` false → \"yes\" on HEAD (Issue8560).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_function_values_and_untyped_params_decayed_dynamic` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}